{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/911777-passion-language-harmony-the-missing-purviews","id":911777,"title":"Passion, Language, Harmony! The Missing Purviews!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-10T11:20:56-07:00","id":911777,"title":"Passion, Language, Harmony! The Missing Purviews!","content":"Basically certain Godly powers are missing.<br /> <br /> Passion, yes the three Epic Socials are powerful, but how does a deity or scion cause one mortal to fall passionately in Love (or hate for that matter) with another mortal?<br /> <br /> Language. I get that the higher level powers for this Purview would require altering, creating, or wiping out whole languages. That's what Fate Binding is for, preventing Power abuse.<br /> <br /> Harmony. We've got Chaos, there were more gods of Harmony and Order than Chaos. Besides, it lets in Music and Kingship as godly themes.<br /> <br /> Reactions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:31:06-07:00","id":911787,"title":"","content":"For 1E, at least, Brent-not-Broken created a Emotion Purview <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/?brk13cte42sd8rm\" target=\"_blank\">here.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:03:15-07:00","id":911808,"title":"","content":"Wasn't Harmony one of the many 1E Virtues?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T23:35:27-07:00","id":912120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/911777-passion-language-harmony-the-missing-purviews#post911777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harmony. We've got Chaos, there were more gods of Harmony and Order than Chaos. Besides, it lets in Music and Kingship as godly themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chaos is supposed to be in opposition to Justice in 1E IIRC. Kingship would undoubtedly fall under it. A Harmony Purview would have problems like Kyman pointed out, it's already a Virtue. The bigger issue I would see is that Harmony, if it were a Purview, would be exceptionally scattered, or be exceptionally rare. A single purview including both Kingship and Music, two huge themes alone, is probably a bit much. Apollo and Marduk are entirely dissimilar entities for example and probably shouldn't share a Purview.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, a whole lot of Music Gods are far from harmonious. Pan, at a thought, is deeply associated with music, and yet totally diverging from any ideas of Harmony. Zeus, though The King without question (as long as you don't ask Hades and Poseidon who will point out they are kings equal to him), has no concerns in the slightest bit about harmony. Zeus just cares about Zeus being king.<br /> <br /> Edit: Random additional note about &quot;but how does a deity or scion cause one mortal to fall passionately in Love (or hate for that matter) with another mortal?&quot; bit. Scion RAW actually addresses this with the Scion of Aphrodite (Donnie Rhodes I think?) has two guns that function like Eros (and Anteros') lead and golden arrows. Instead of making an entire Purview to solve the problem, I've found that following in this idea is easier. (Though, little note. Eros and Anteros' arrows are a terrifying political tool. Like, you can sew utter chaos through Pantheons with things like that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-11-2016, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:15:45-07:00","id":912294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/911777-passion-language-harmony-the-missing-purviews?p=912120#post912120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Random additional note about &quot;but how does a deity or scion cause one mortal to fall passionately in Love (or hate for that matter) with another mortal?&quot; bit. Scion RAW actually addresses this with the Scion of Aphrodite (Donnie Rhodes I think?) has two guns that function like Eros (and Anteros') lead and golden arrows. Instead of making an entire Purview to solve the problem, I've found that following in this idea is easier. (Though, little note. Eros and Anteros' arrows are a terrifying political tool. Like, you can sew utter chaos through Pantheons with things like that.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Like tossing around gilded fruit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:53:20-07:00","id":912313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/911777-passion-language-harmony-the-missing-purviews?p=912294#post912294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like tossing around gilded fruit...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's what I get for writing posts at 3am, forgetting the biggest example of item-based emotional manipulation for the Theoi. I have never had one of those show up in one of our games, but I would dread it. A single one ended the Age of Heroes for the Theoi, just a whole lotta don't want to deal with one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:05:22-07:00","id":912324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/911777-passion-language-harmony-the-missing-purviews?p=912313#post912313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's what I get for writing posts at 3am, forgetting the biggest example of item-based emotional manipulation for the Theoi. I have never had one of those show up in one of our games, but I would dread it. A single one ended the Age of Heroes for the Theoi, just a whole lotta don't want to deal with one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely seems like it goes beyond what Relics of the likes Donnie-as-a-Hero is carrying around should be capable of....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:18:32-07:00","id":912372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/911777-passion-language-harmony-the-missing-purviews?p=911808#post911808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't Harmony one of the many 1E Virtues?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. So another name would be needed. But just as there is a Chaos Purview an Order/Harmony Purview seems right/logical. Maybe it would be called the Music Purview, Divine musicians are about the harmony of the universe generally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:12:15-07:00","id":912473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/911777-passion-language-harmony-the-missing-purviews?p=912372#post912372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. So another name would be needed. But just as there is a Chaos Purview an Order/Harmony Purview seems right/logical. Maybe it would be called the Music Purview, Divine musicians are about the harmony of the universe generally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Justice is supposed to be the Purview set in opposition to Chaos. Their names don't really click, but mythical Chaos has a lot more to do with social disorder than randomness for example. That social disorder is opposed by social order, which is Justice. Your divine monarchs (Zeus, Marduk, Amaterasu, Shango), and judges (Wyandot-Wolf Deity), resist this social disorder through the application of law or other law-like tradition.<br /> <br /> I will admit to be horrifically undereducated in the Pantheons east of the Tigris, but the Deities associated with Music I know of don't necessarily have much to do with the harmony of the Universe. Pan, and Apollo both don't do much with balancing or keeping the world in harmony (Apollo does have something to do with civilization I think? Ajax is better at the Theoi than I am) for the Theoi. Cairbre the Bard from the Tuatha provoked a colossal civil war by single handedly usurping Bres through devising the first satire. For the Aztecs (Griff knows them far better than I do though) their two deities linked with music (Huehuecoyotl and Xochipilli) are both exceptionally disharmonious. (Huehuecoyotl is a trickster coyote figure, while Xochipilli is all about hallucinogenic mushrooms and homosexual... prostitutes I think? Both of which are Not-Good-Things to the Aztecs)<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh yeah, and then there are the Thunder-Drummers, Shango and Raijin. I wouldn't quite say that Shango is harmonious save for the fact he brings stability through being exceptionally invested in Shango being King. Raijin is theoretically currently under the sway of Kannon and thereby calm and gentle, but naturally he is dangerous and destructive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-11-2016, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:27:36-07:00","id":913715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/911777-passion-language-harmony-the-missing-purviews#post911777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically certain Godly powers are missing.<br /> <br /> Passion, yes the three Epic Socials are powerful, but how does a deity or scion cause one mortal to fall passionately in Love (or hate for that matter) with another mortal?<br /> <br /> Language. I get that the higher level powers for this Purview would require altering, creating, or wiping out whole languages. That's what Fate Binding is for, preventing Power abuse.<br /> <br /> Harmony. We've got Chaos, there were more gods of Harmony and Order than Chaos. Besides, it lets in Music and Kingship as godly themes.<br /> <br /> Reactions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Harmony is a Virtue, and Justice is the purview that opposes Chaos.<br /> <br /> Justice was the purview that dealt with social order, laws and.consequences","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T11:44:40-07:00","id":916930,"title":"","content":"What would the general reaction to a &quot;Smith/Forge&quot; purview be? Passion and Language seem to pass muster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T13:35:41-07:00","id":916968,"title":"","content":"That one is totally needed. It simply comes up far, far too often for it not to exist as a Purview. More often than Illusion, and Frost in the very least. Hephaestus, Ptah, Goibniu, Wayland, Daedalus, Svarog, and more in the realm of simply smiting, though a Purview could easily include all arts, or just the more physical ones like carpentry.<br /> <br /> There have been several goes to create a Forge Purview, including Gotham by Night's Artistry (which has been taken down, but included powers for less physical arts like music), and Telgar's <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GphJd2M0fW2avXCTglLYT738bH8uqlOmM9hZCjpDBtw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Forge Purview</a>. Forge / Smith / Art is a big missing piece from Scion 1E, which you are very right does need to be houseruled in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T18:56:17-07:00","id":917091,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in Scion 1E, it seemed like only the Dodekatheon were capable of producing real crafters thanks to their &quot;super skill&quot; Purview.<br /> <br /> The Egyptians definitely require a purview to help with crafting, seeing as their monuments have existed thousands of years after their empire collapsed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T19:18:30-07:00","id":917098,"title":"","content":"1ed.Left crafting to supernatural races. Aesir-Dwarves, Theoi-Cyclops, Kami-Tengu, etc. I figure since (mechanically) you only got to actually acquire relics 3 times in your scion career, the ability to get them was ultra rare. So just allowing a player to head to his forge and churn out relics in between adventures was not part of how they envisioned the game. <br /> <br /> And to be fair I'm rather interested in how they are going to go about balancing this purview. If I just take the table on page 151 of Scion Companion and say something along the lines of you can do this stuff but you need to be capable of doing it to put it into an item (e.g. you'd have to be Leg 6 to produce a power that mimicked a 5th level boon) then I can see a lot of people wanting to take this purview and just making themselves awesome weapons/armour/items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T20:42:51-07:00","id":917141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/911777-passion-language-harmony-the-missing-purviews?p=916930#post916930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would the general reaction to a &quot;Smith/Forge&quot; purview be? Passion and Language seem to pass muster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artistry is definitely a purview that needs to exist in some capacity, since there are a huge number of concepts that can fill that design space. Gotham By Night has a version that works pretty well, and Telgar wrote one up a while back (as Watcher mentioned).<br /> <br /> Passion is also a moderately decent purview, though everyone disagrees with how it should function and what boons it should have.<br /> <br /> Language does not pass muster as a purview.<br /> <br /> Music as been brought up as a purview before, but there is not enough meat to fill out an entire purview.<br /> <br /> Conversely, there is more than enough meat to fill out a Wealth purview, but there is not much need. Just a few boons in other purviews can suffice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}